# Template for /etc/cairn-updater.env — installed root:root 0600.
#
# This file is a template and stays one: it never carries a real token, in this
# repository or in the copy the installer writes. Both values below are empty
# and the helper refuses to start while they are, so an installation that was
# never finished by hand fails closed instead of running with a guessable
# credential.
#
# The operator fills both, by hand, on the host:
#
#   umask 077
#   printf 'DEPLOY_AUTH_TOKEN=%s\n' "$(openssl rand -base64 48 | tr -d '\n')" \
#     >> /etc/cairn-updater.env
#
# The token must be at least 32 characters; cmd/cairn-updater refuses anything
# shorter. There is no development exemption for an empty value.

# Bearer credential for the four /api/deploy/system/* routes. Nothing else on
# the host holds it: Caddy proxies without a credential, and the webtag account
# cannot read this file.
DEPLOY_AUTH_TOKEN=

# Host connection string for the PostgreSQL container's loopback mapping, e.g.
# postgres://webtag:...@127.0.0.1:5432/webtag?sslmode=disable
# The helper needs it for the pre-migration dump and for the target release's
# migrate run. It is not the same string the application uses only insofar as
# the application may use a different account; both must be host URLs, because
# neither this helper nor the application gets Docker socket access.
DATABASE_URL=

# Everything below is optional and defaults to the production layout compiled
# into cmd/cairn-updater/config.go. Uncomment only to move a path, and then
# re-run the installer so the units and the permission model move with it.
#CAIRN_UPDATER_SOCKET=/run/cairn-updater.sock
#CAIRN_UPDATER_SOCKET_GROUP=caddy
#CAIRN_UPDATER_STATE_DIR=/var/lib/cairn-updater
#CAIRN_UPDATER_CORE_DIR=/opt/webtag
#CAIRN_UPDATER_READER_DIR=/var/www/reader
#CAIRN_UPDATER_ENV_FILE=/etc/cairn-updater.env
#CAIRN_UPDATER_SERVICE=webtag.service
#CAIRN_UPDATER_SERVICE_USER=webtag
#CAIRN_UPDATER_HEALTH_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8732
#CAIRN_UPDATER_PG_DUMP=pg_dump
#CAIRN_UPDATER_PG_RESTORE=pg_restore
#CAIRN_UPDATER_MIN_FREE_BYTES=2147483648
